{"study_accession":"PRJNA1014459","secondary_study_accession":"SRP459362","title":"Mitochondrial N-formylmethionine instructs tissue-inflammatory CD4+ T cells by redirecting endolysosomal pathways","description":"Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is a T-cell dependent autoimmune disease that causes tissue damaging joint inflammation. Mechanisms through which T cells from RA patients mediate tissue injury are poorly understood, but one of their distinguishing features is their poor mitochondrial performance. We performed RNAseq analysis of stimulated CD4+ T cells from 8 RA (ATPlow) and 8 RA (ATPint) patients. CD4+ T cells from RA (ATPlow) (n=4 each) were stimulated and treated with vehicle or the mPTP inhibitor CsA (5uM).CD4+ T cells from RA (ATPint) (n=4 each) were stimulated and treated with vehicle or the fMet (5 ng/ml) for 24 hrs Overall design: We performed RNAseq analysis of stimulated CD4+ T cells from four RA (ATPlow) and four RA (ATPint) patients. CD4+ T cells from RA (ATPlow) (n=4 each) were stimulated and treated with vehicle or the mPTP inhibitor CsA (5uM).CD4+ T cells from RA (ATPint) (n=4 each) were stimulated and treated with vehicle or the fMet (5 ng/ml) for 24 hrs","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":16,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN37331255","study_accession":"PRJNA1014459","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"CD4+t CELLS, RA (ATPLOW)-4,CSA","description":"CD4+t CELLS, RA (ATPLOW)-4,CSA","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7770059","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-09-21","attributes":[["source_name","pbmc"],["tissue","pbmc"],["cell_type","cd3+cd28+ stimulated cd4+t"],["disease","RA (ATPlow)"],["genotype","ra"],["treatment","csa"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25987911","experiment_accession":"SRX21706297","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":32420714,"base_count":9726214200,"first_public":"